  "goodToKnow": "Die Weltwirtschaftskrise usually means the Great Depression, which began with the New York crash of October 1929 (Schwarzer Donnerstag). In Germany, unemployment rose to about six million by 1932, and the mass misery helped the Nazis to power. The 2008–09 financial crisis was also called a Weltwirtschaftskrise. Die Wirtschaft means economy. Plural: die Weltwirtschaftskrisen."
